  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pollicy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pollicy and partners

Rapid Research For Agile Policy Making: Building on the foundation of thr ongoing project, &quot;Rapid Research For Agile Policy Making,&quot; the next phase responds to the urgent challenges posed by the recently enacted Anti HomosexualityAct in Uganda. This legislative shift introduces new and heightens the already existent physical and digital legal and safety concerns for LGBTQ+ rights organizations, necessitating an evolved approach to the work of the consortium. However, within thesechallenges lie uniqueopportunities to enhance digital safety, leverage technology for human rights promotion, and strengthen legal partnerships for effective response.
In the next year, the project will strategically aim not only to mitigate the negativeimpacts of the legislative changes but also to further empower the rights holders to sustainably navigate the evolving landscape and contribute meaningfully to policymaking and transparency as we continue to pursue equity and justice. This will be donethrough a combination of activities: continuing research and mapping, development of guides and strengthening of the data collaborative platform with new analysis, advocacy and communications, and linking and learning.</narrative>
  </description>
